, 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': ' '}, {'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': ' Ah, the user is correcting me! It seems `app_next` is actually the OLD Next.js app, not the new TanStack app. And the `app` directory is the new TanStack structure. Let me re-verify which is which.'}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'functions.Bash:6', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'head -5 app/package.json 2>/dev/null || echo \"No package.json in app/\"', 'description': 'Check app/package.json'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'functions.Bash:7', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'head -5 app_next/package.json 2>/dev/null|| echo \"No package.json in app_next/\"', 'description': 'Check app_next/package.json'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'functions.Bash:8', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'ls app/ | head -10', 'description': 'List files in app/'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'functions.Bash:9', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'ls app_next/ | head -10', 'description': 'List files in app_next/'}}], 'reasoning_content': None}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'functions.Bash:6', 'content': 'No package.json in app/'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'functions.Bash:7', 'content': 'No package.json in app_next/'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'functions.Bash:8', 'content': '__root.jsx\\napi\\nblog\\ncontact.jsx\\nglobals.css\\nindex.jsx\\nprojects\\nresume.jsx\\nstack.jsx'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'functions.Bash:9', 'content': 'api\\nblog\\ncontact\\nerror.jsx\\nlayout.jsx\\npage.jsx\\nprojects\\nresume\\nrobot.js\\nsitemap.js'}], 'reasoning_content': None}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': ' '}, {'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': ' Good, so now I understand:\\n- `app/` contains the new TanStack app (single route files like contact.jsx, resume.jsx, etc.)\\n- `app_next/` contains the old Next.js app (with Next.js conventions like layout.jsx, page.jsx, sitemap.js, etc.)\\n\\nSo in the current